Pr Ext(c, tr) ̸= M : r ← RndH , c = CommitH (M, r) ≤ εext ,
where tr is the query–answer trace of this run of Rnd and Commit, and the probability is over H and the
random choices of Rnd.
Definition 2.10 (Extractability of the commitment, no two openings). Let Π, Ext and H be as in
Definition 2.9 and εop : N → [0, ∞]. A pair (M, r) opens a commitment c if CommitH (M, r) = c; the queries of
this test are not counted in qC , qO or q. Probabilities are over H and the algorithms’ random choices.
1. Π has extractability of the commitment (also called opening-form binding) for Ext with error εop if,
for every qC -query algorithm AC that outputs a commitment c and a state, with trace trC , and every
qO -query algorithm that outputs a pair (M, r) given this state,
