Remark 2.11 (Standard names). No two openings is the standard binding property of a commitment
scheme [CFQ19, Definition 2.1], for (Rnd, Commit). Extractability of the commitment is the property
that [BCS16, Section 3.1] calls extractability; correctness of extraction is its form for the honest committer’s
own input.
Definition 2.12 (Completeness on a set of triples). Let Π = (Rnd, Commit, P, V ) be a commit-and-prove
argument (Definition 2.6) for the indexed relation Rel, S a set of triples (M, x, y), and α ∈ [0, 1]. The argument
Π is complete on S with error α if, for every (M, x, y) ∈ S ∩ Rel,
