Remark 5.12 (Committer-chosen weights). As in every commit-and-prove argument, the committer chooses
the weights. By itself, Theorem 5.11 therefore excludes nothing against a committer who commits to weights
under which every output meets the policy. Such weights exist for many policies: under all-zero weights,
every non-empty output that fits one window together with a non-empty prompt, all tokens in V, meets every
policy with θ, C ≥ 257 (Proposition 3.9). The theorem constrains a provider only together with correctness of
extraction at the same extractor (Definition 2.9; for the explicit committer, Theorem 5.17) and with knowledge
of who made the commitment (Limitation 8.7, Unattributed commitment). At exact match it also excludes
an accepted empty output (Proposition 3.5).

