Remark 6.10 (Not a statement on the weights). Theorem 6.9 concerns one of the three provers, at the default
configuration’s size, which every admissible Z has. By part 1, to an honest verifier the link proof’s messages
add nothing to what the two tables’ OOD answers and opened columns show. These are computed from the
weights and the tables’ randomness (on their distribution: Theorem 6.3), so by itself part 1 does not state that
the weights are hidden. Part 1 extends Corollary 6.7 to Plink , with the other two provers constant-message
provers, at (dg, par) = (0λ , ∅), values at which VZ is not proved ever to be called (Corollary C.29). Nor is it
proved at these values that the compiled verifier accepts Plink ; on acceptance after compilation: Section 6.5.

