What has run under each policy

Exact match requires that the integer model itself be served: of the 96 greedy outputs of each of two
floating-point engines (16-bit, FP8), none matched the integer model’s greedy token at every token position
(scored without proofs† ). A vLLM plug-in is designed to serve it, one request at a time: not on the released
programs† , on the public weights and one H100, beside a helper process, it took 0.58 to 0.63 seconds per
token after prompts of at most 5 tokens, and 0.58 to 1.46 over all 48 outputs. Clipped-gap parameters fitted
on honest greedy outputs accept most outputs with one token replaced (Table 5) and most sampled outputs,
86 of 96 at temperature 0.7 and 85 of 96 with top-p 0.9 (scored likewise, 16-bit fit) (Limitation 8.8, Clipped
gap is weak). Serving and proving have not run together as one service (Appendix H.4).

