Remark A.26 (Round counts). Table 10 is read off several machine-checked lemmas on reductions of the Lean library.
It is not one Lean statement, and the proof of Theorem 5.1 uses only the common count of Lemma A.28. For Masked
sumcheck, Fold, the Code switch of a Proximity test, Base case and Range test, Lean proves that the reduction leads
(Definition A.18) from the reduction’s condition to the relation that its witness map sends each witness of the output’s
claims to one of the input’s. For OOD seeds and positions it proves the count alone; for Batching and Lookup the
entries are the counts that Lean compares with 2−128 .
Six rows follow in form, as counts for this protocol’s codes and not term for term, error terms of [CFW26, version
of February 25, 2026]: OOD seeds, the first error of its Lemma 9.9; the two rows on Fold, the errors of its Lemma 6.5;
Positions, the spot checks in its Lemmas 7.4 and 9.9; Code switch in a Proximity test, the other two errors of its
Lemma 9.9 (in its overview, the second error of Lemma 2.17); Base case, the first error of its Lemma 7.4.
Of the two rows on Masked sumcheck, the first, on the challenge that joins mask and claim, has the form of the
first error of [CFW26, version of February 25, 2026, Lemma 6.5], and the count for the further variable of the second,
sampled off one point (there, off two), that of the third error of its Theorem 11.3, each without the list sizes; the count
for the other variables is that of a sumcheck round [LFKN92].

