B

Further statements and proofs for Section 5

Here, in Appendix C and Appendix D, and at Proposition 3.12, Lemma 4.9, Lemma 4.18, Lemma 5.13, and Lemma A.35,
some machine-checked statements have neither a printed proof nor an outline. Their ground is the kernel’s check of
the Lean statements that Appendix F names for them.
Proposition B.1 (Policies that every eligible output meets). [machine-checked] Let µ be valid model parameters
(Definition 3.6) and pol = (C, θ, cap) an acceptance policy (Definition 3.4).
1. If MF ≤ KF + 11 and θ, C ≥ 2436593409, then, for all weights M , every output that is eligible under M meets
pol under M . The policy (232 − 1, 2436593409, 0) is an instance.
2. Let µ = µZ0 (Definition 3.8), θ ≤ C < 232 and 1 ≤ nct ≤ L − 1. Then θ = C and cap ≥ nct if and only if, for
all weights M , every output with nct counted tokens that is eligible under M meets pol under M .
Remark B.2 (All weights). What a clipped-gap policy excludes depends on the committed weights and on numbers
that the provider writes into Z.
1. Up to cap counted tokens may be any tokens, where the others leave room in the sum (Remark 3.10, What a
policy bounds).
2. Some policies of admissible configurations exclude no token (Proposition B.1). VZ does not reject a configuration
with such a policy, and the C++ verifier rejects some such policies but not every one: no verifier sees the model’s
logits.
3. At MF ≤ KF + 11 some threshold of a configuration with these exponents, if it is admissible (which has been
evaluated at three parameter sets, not proved), excludes no token, whatever the weights; the C++ verifier never
prints these two exponents.
4. The weights by which the proof of Proposition B.1 violates a policy are synthetic. Nothing follows for a trained
model, under whose weights every eligible output may still meet such a policy.
Proposition B.3 (The example clipped-gap policy). [machine-checked] Let pol = (25856, 512, 1), the policy of
Z1 (Definition 3.7), let µ be valid model parameters and M ∈ I, and let y be an output that is eligible on a prompt x
under M , with nct counted tokens and logit gaps gapi (Definition 3.4).
1. If y meets pol and nct ≤ 99, then gapi < 25600 for all i < nct , and

