The last four rows do not come from lean/CREDITS.md or from its table of files. The row on [CFW26] rests on
a mark that stood at the head of Lean files while the library was written. The mark named no title; we read it as
meaning that work. It was set on groups of files, in some directories on every file, and for a time on every new file, and
it passed to files that a program made from marked ones; so it may name more files than were written from that work,
and it does not show, file by file, what a file’s writer had at hand.
The row on [CFWpc] is over files that comments in the Lean files tie to that work, and over files that state, prove
or use the definitions of the Lean files that follow or render it. The row after it is over files that do not count as
written independently of that work. The last row is over the files adapted from ArkLib, which that page lists too, and

