two on one machine and commitment, one directly after the other, differed by at most 0.26 % (111.64 and 111.35
tokens/second). Three runs of the same kind on other programs, on other machines on another day, gave 105.3
± 3.9 tokens/second (100.85 to 108.06); among their six executions two such differed by 6.3 %† of the larger
(111.55 and 104.56 tokens/second). No cause is shown for either; the released programs did not run on those
machines, nor the other programs on the timed runs’. A gap between rows that is no larger is uninformative.
Apart from the clipped-gap row and its control, which ran in pairs on one machine and commitment, the rows

