the kernel checks proofs, not evaluations. Some runs evaluated the executable form directly, in a separate build of the
executable form, tied to VZ by name and statement, not by bytes; the lean-verify command was not used for them.
That build’s Lean files are not shown to be the released ones; it alone made the decisions that Table 4 marks as by a
separate build of the executable form, among them its side of the 43 comparisons and of the four matched alterations.
No theorem covers any of these parsers.

